# Changelog

All notable changes to the **Kasi-Tech Solutions** website will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/),
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).

---

## [Unreleased]

### Planned
- Image optimisation (WebP format + responsive sizes)
- Optional FAQ or blog section
- Standardise all internal file paths and filenames (case consistency)

---

## [1.1.0] - 2026-10-25

### Added
- Integrated **EmailJS SDK** (`v3`) into both `contactus.html` and `enquiry.html` for asynchronous, backend-free form submissions.
- Implemented a unified JavaScript validation script (`validation.js`) supporting both form pages with custom inline red error messaging and dynamic error clearing.
- Added custom CSS error styling (`.input-error` borders and `.error-message` spans) for enhanced user feedback and form accessibility.

### Fixed
- Fixed input `name` attribute mapping (`fullName`, `email`, `mobileNumber`, `subject`) across both forms to synchronize seamlessly with EmailJS template variables.
- Disabled browser default validation popup bubbles using `novalidate` to maintain a consistent custom error UI.

---

## [1.0.0] - 2026-09-17

### Added
- Initial release of the Kasi-Tech Solutions company website (`www.Kasi-Techsolutions.co.za`).
- **Home page** (`index.html`) with hero banner, service highlights, and call-to-action.
- **About Us page** with company history, mission, vision, and team profiles.
- **Services page** showcasing Web Application, Network Infrastructure, and Database & System Analysis.
- **Enquiry page** with consultation/quotation request form and preferred availability options.
- **Contact Us page** with callback form, contact details, opening hours, and embedded Google Map.
- Responsive CSS stylesheet (`style.css`) using CSS custom properties, Flexbox, and Grid.
- Multi-column footer with brand info, helpful links, contact details, and social media icons.
- Font Awesome 6.5.1 icons integration.
- Consistent branding (navy blue primary + gold accent colour scheme).
- Mobile-friendly navigation and layout (breakpoints at 900px and 600px).

### Team Credits
- Somila Manentsa – IT Manager & Systems Analyst
- Landile Mbuti – Infrastructure Specialist
- Asavela Ngcamla – Database Architect
- Kubobonke Diko – Web Systems Developer

